===Etymology 1===
{{ety|en|id=stylus|:inh|enm:stile<id:style>|tree=1}}
The noun is derived from {{inh|en|enm|stile|t=writing tool; piece of written work; characteristic mode of expression; demeanour; person's designation or title; stem of a plant; period of time}} (compare semantic development to {{m|ru|по́черк|t=handwriting, style}}),<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=stīle|pos=''n.''(2)|noformat=yes|id=MED42945|accessdate=20 July 2019}}</ref> from {{der|en|fro|estile}}, or from {{der|en|la-med|stylus}}, both from {{der|en|la|stilus|t=pointed instrument; writing tool; composition; characteristic mode of expression; stem of a plant}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*(s)teyg-|t=to be sharp; to pierce, prick, puncture, stab; to goad}}.<ref name="OED">Compare {{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=192315|date=1919}}</ref><ref>{{cite-web|url=https://www.lexico.com/definition/style|title=Style|publisher=Lexico|date=September 26, 2021|accessdate=25 January 2023|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210926142256/https://www.lexico.com/definition/style|archivedate=26 September 2021}}</ref> {{doublet|en|stylus}}.

The verb is derived from the noun.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=v|id=192316|date=1919|nodot=yes}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=v}}</ref>

